  "as_of": "2022-07-27",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would clarify how Self-Employment Assistance payments are treated under family law, social security and veterans’ legislation, aligning them with existing self-employment support payments.",
   "It would update program definitions and references so established maintenance, child support and benefit calculation rules continue to apply to participants receiving these payments.",
   "The main changes would begin on royal assent, with technical social security corrections starting the following day and future program renaming handled through public notice."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Family law regulations would expressly list Self-Employment Assistance payments as an income-tested pension, allowance or benefit.",
   "Social security law would use a self-employment program definition covering both the new program and the New Enterprise Incentive Scheme.",
   "The Employment Secretary would have to notify any change to the program’s name by notifiable instrument."
  ],
  "affected": "Self-Employment Assistance participants, and parents and other parties whose entitlements are considered in family law maintenance and child support matters, are affected.",
